    "body": "I described more such cases in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10488 and my initial understanding is that this PR would fix these too. This sounds reasonable to me, but I'm no longer employed at Mozilla. \r\n\r\nTherefore this PR impacts [these tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/4df85d1ac95ee7f6fb685055ba16ce91e5d0b876/html/dom/elements/global-attributes/dir-slots-directionality.html#L162-L226) that are currently [passing](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/dom/elements/global-attributes/dir-slots-directionality.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=dir-slots-directionality.html) in Chromium, so Chromiums implementation might not be fully compliant with this spec change.",
