    "created_at": "2024-08-19T14:09:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-19T14:09:19Z",
    "body": "One further note here:  there are effectively two sub-parts to the change:\r\n\r\n1. skipping the excluded elements (bdi, script, style, textarea, element with dir attribute) when they're assigned nodes in a slot\r\n2. not applying the special rules intended to affect dir=auto only on an element itself but not on ancestors (for auto-directionality form-associated elements and for slots) on the assigned nodes in a slot when computing dir=auto for the slot\r\n\r\nChange (1) requires code updates in both Gecko and Chromium; change (2) matches current Chromium code but requires code updates in Gecko (and one WPT update).\r\n\r\nI just wrote the Chromium code change for (1), so after I compile it I'll figure out what WPT updates are needed.  Then I'll separately prepare the WPT updates for change (2) as well (which as far as current tests affect just one test where Gecko and Chromium disagree).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
